librist source pin
==================

`./src` is **pristine upstream librist** at tag:

    v0.2.20
    repo https://code.videolan.org/rist/librist.git

`src/` carries no `.git`: it is a plain vendored tree so it can be tracked by this
repository.

Every open-broadcast change is a patch in this directory, applied to the copy in
`$(PKG_BUILD_DIR)` by `Build/Prepare` (`$(Build/Patch)`, `PATCH_DIR` defaults to
`./patches`):

| patch | scope |
|---|---|
| `001-librist-receiver-fixes.patch` | Two upstream-quality librist bug fixes (not product-specific -- worth upstreaming): **`src/rist-common.c`** fixes `rist_peer_recv_wrap` so the receive loop runs at least once on Windows. **`src/udp.c`** stops double-counting data bandwidth -- `rist_calculate_bitrate()` was called in the RTCP path *and* by its callers. |
| `002-rist2rist-wan-telemetry.patch` | The open-broadcast feature and its hardening: the `rist2rist` proxy emits its **WAN-leg** link quality back to the encoder over **RIST OOB** (`RIST_OOB_API_IP_IDENT_TELEMETRY` = 54322, `tools/oob_shared.[ch]` + `tools/rist2rist.c`) -- this is what the encoder's `bitrate_source::remote_oob` adaptive-bitrate source consumes, so it is REQUIRED when the encoder sends through this bridge. Includes: a telemetry mutex (libRIST runs a separate sender and receiver protocol thread per context, so the telemetry globals *were* raced), SIGTERM handling, the hot-path `assert` replaced by a NULL check, the master relay loop's `ret < 0` backoff, the mixed-profile `--out-profile` support, and the stats-JSON dump moved INFO -> DEBUG. |

History
-------

The pin was previously an untagged master snapshot (commit `6377b5c`,
"Merge branch 'feature/prometheus-avg-buffer-time' into 'master'", reporting
itself as 0.2.18) -- the upstream tree the `patcarter883/librist` fork was based
on. It moved to the v0.2.20 RELEASE for a reproducible, tagged base.

`001` originally carried a third fix: replacing
`assert(packet_time < next->packet_time)` in the retry-interpolation path with a
clamp, to stop a VBR source SIGABRTing the process. **Upstream removed that
assert**, so the hunk no longer applies and has been dropped -- the fix is now
upstream's. If a future rebase reintroduces a FAILED hunk here, check whether
upstream has adopted the fix before re-adding it.

Regenerating
------------

Only the patches named in `series` are applied -- that is why this README is safe
sitting here. Add a new patch to BOTH this directory and `series`, or it will be
silently ignored.

Do **not** edit `./src` and commit the result -- that reintroduces the untracked
embedded-repo problem this layout exists to fix. Edit a scratch copy of librist,
then regenerate:

    git -C <librist checkout> diff <base-commit> -- <files> > patches/00N-....patch

Verify a patch still applies and reproduces the intended tree before committing it:

    patch -p1 --dry-run -d <pristine copy> < patches/00N-....patch

The WAN-telemetry feature this patch originally carried (a `wan_telemetry_t` struct written back to
the encoder over RIST OOB as ident 54322, for observing per-leg quality while debugging the bonded
balancing) has been REMOVED -- it was debug scaffolding, and its only consumer was the encoder's
`rist_oob_cb`. The UCI `telemetry_enabled` / `telemetry_target` options, the LuCI "Enable WAN Stats
Telemetry" controls and the rpcd `telemetry` field went with it.

NOTE: the ROUTER-SIDE telemetry config (`telemetry_enabled` / `telemetry_target` in UCI, the LuCI
"Enable WAN Stats Telemetry" controls, and the rpcd `telemetry` field) has been REMOVED. That was a
rist2rist remote-logging (`-r`) push of its logs/stats to an external UDP collector, used only while
debugging the multi-WAN bonding. It is NOT the same thing as the RIST OOB back-channel above, which
stays. The `rtt_hysteresis` UCI option went too -- nothing ever read it.
